# void-harness:end

# Session telemetry written by the SHIPPED hook bundle, which predates the
# three-level layout and still writes to the flat paths. What it observes now
# belongs under .void/machine/, and the sources already write there; until a
# published bundle carries that change, these two paths stay uncovered by the
# managed block and a plain `git add .` would commit session telemetry.
#
# Kept OUTSIDE the markers because `void-harness init` rewrites everything
# between them. Every consumer project has the same uncovered paths today.
# Removing these lines is safe only once the shipped bundle writes to machine/.
.void/runs/
.void/outputs/

.gstack/
dist-singlefile/
